Title: Enable the ANGLE D3D9 fallback by default
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Without this the GPU process dies at startup on Windows Vista, and the reported
symptom points nowhere near the cause: "Initialization of all (1) EGL display
types failed", with the GL implementation already demoted to SwiftShader before
the display loop ran.

GetDisplayTypes() in ui/gl/init/gl_display_initializer.cc builds the default
ANGLE chain as D3D11, then D3D9 only if features::IsANGLED3D9FallbackAllowed().
Upstream ships that feature disabled -- reasonably, since the oldest Windows it
supports always has D3D11, and there is a standing intent to delete the D3D9
backend (crbug.com/40874754). Vista without the Platform Update has no
d3d11.dll at all, so the chain is D3D11 and nothing else; D3D11 fails, the GPU
process falls back to SwiftShader, SwiftShader fails too, and the process is
gone. D3D9 works on Vista the whole time. Nothing was choosing it.

Enabling it by default is close to free. AddInitDisplay() only *appends* D3D9
behind D3D11, so wherever D3D11 initialises -- every Windows version this
feature was disabled for -- D3D9 is never attempted. The behaviour only differs
where the alternative is no GPU process at all.

This is why the feature is flipped here rather than in
patches/chromium/ui/0007-remove-d3d9-angle-backend-support-from-chromium.patch,
which reintroduces the line: that series is reverts of upstream removals and is
kept verbatim so it stays mechanical to rebase. patches/other/ applies last.

Related: kFallbackToSWIfGLES3NotSupported is already disabled on Windows
upstream, specifically "for D3D9 users that are still on ES 2", which is
exactly this configuration -- D3D9 caps at ES 2.0, and gl_context_egl.cc
retries 3.0 as 2.0 and succeeds. The EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE errors logged along the
way are noise; a genuinely failed retry logs "Fallback eglCreateContext ES 2.0
failed" instead.

diff --git a/ui/gl/gl_features.cc b/ui/gl/gl_features.cc
index d7ef4195d1..bbfaf97c9e 100644
--- a/ui/gl/gl_features.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/gl_features.cc
@@ -115,7 +115,14 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kDefaultPassthroughCommandDecoder,
 // Controls whether the GPU process falls back to software if GLES3 is not
 // supported.
 BASE_FEATURE(kFallbackToSWIfGLES3NotSupported,
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+             // TODO(https://crbug.com/444049511): Currently disabled on
+             // Windows for D3D9 users that are still on ES 2. Enable once
+             // crbug.com/40874754 is fixed, deprecating D3D9 usage.
+             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+#else   // BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
@@ -320,7 +327,7 @@ bool IsSwiftShaderUsedForWebGLByCommandLine(
 
 // Allow fallback to SwfitShader without command line flags during the
 // deprecation period.
-BASE_FEATURE(kAllowSwiftShaderFallback, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+BASE_FEATURE(kAllowSwiftShaderFallback, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 bool IsSwiftShaderAllowedByFeature() {
   return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kAllowSwiftShaderFallback);
@@ -364,7 +371,7 @@ bool IsAnySoftwareGLAllowed(const base::CommandLine* command_line) {
 }
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kAllowSoftwareGLFallbackDueToCrashes,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 bool IsSoftwareGLFallbackDueToCrashesAllowed(
     const base::CommandLine* command_line) {
@@ -375,6 +382,23 @@ bool IsSoftwareGLFallbackDueToCrashesAllowed(
   return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kAllowSoftwareGLFallbackDueToCrashes);
 }
 
+// Enabled here, disabled upstream. This only appends ANGLE_D3D9 to the list of
+// display types to try, after ANGLE_D3D11 -- see GetDisplayTypes() in
+// ui/gl/init/gl_display_initializer.cc -- so on anything where D3D11
+// initialises, which is every Windows this feature was turned off for, D3D9 is
+// never reached and the default costs nothing.
+//
+// It is not free to leave off. Vista has no D3D11 at all without the Platform
+// Update, so with the fallback disabled the list holds D3D11 alone, that fails,
+// and the GPU process skips to SwiftShader and dies there -- reported as
+// "Initialization of all (1) EGL display types failed". D3D9 works on Vista;
+// nothing was selecting it.
+BASE_FEATURE(kAllowANGLED3D9Fallback, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+
+bool IsANGLED3D9FallbackAllowed() {
+  return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kAllowANGLED3D9Fallback);
+}
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
 BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidLimitRgb565DisplayToApi32,
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
